body:
Hi,

Thanks for reporting.

@zzzeek since the new system is based on the assumption that the constraints are always at the end, I'm not sure it can be adapted to support the fact that constraints can appear also between column definitions. Maybe it causes less issues reverting it, at least until we have a better system that's not based on regexp?

@CaselIT i just spent an hour with the regex, trying to use two regexes, agree we need to revert the regex for  #11832 as well as #11677, however we also need to add the test above as well as maintain the tests that were added for #11832 and #11677 but mark them as failing

SQLite documentation here if it does not already needs to include notes that constraint reflection can only handle constraints that are either on a full newline by themselves or are inline with a column definition but include no newlines of their own

cc @jeffh92 unfortunately we need to fully revert the code changes you made in efa344b as the regular expression approach here still fails to handle simple scenarios
